# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 3: mori), edited.

~ start
Narrator: The parlor smells of beeswax and cold tin. Mori opens a cedar drawer of brass coffin plates.
mori_shade [sad]: I stencil these for the Order of the Oak, though the folks named on them still walk the streets.
* Ask who ordered them -> who
* Look at the list -> list
* Ask whether one of ours who has fallen can be called back -> wickermoor/mori_shade:raising_gate
* Leave -> END

~ who
mori_shade [weary]: On the first of each month, a folded slip and a silver piece wait beneath my door.
mori_shade [sad]: A man must keep his fires lit, so I oil my punches and do not watch the threshold.
-> start

~ list
Narrator: Five brass plates lie nested in black velvet, each stamped with neat, square letters.
mori_shade [afraid]: Geneva Fairchild, Howie Butterman, Ambrose Quill, Finneas Trout. The fifth was ordered polished, but left blank.
set mori_list_seen
quest what_mori_keeps asked
-> decide

~ decide
mori_shade [weary]: My hands shake with every letter. You are strangers, unburdened by our customs: tell me what to do.
* Warn the named villagers -> warn
* Burn the list -> burn
* Give the list to Doris Squire -> doris
* Say nothing, and ask him to keep working -> silent

~ warn
Narrator: Word travels the lanes faster than moor mist, leaving shuttered windows and bolted doors behind.
mori_shade [sad]: They cross the mud to avoid my shop, whispering the undertaker wishes them cold. Perhaps they are right.
set mori_outcome = "warn"
standing cult -1
quest what_mori_keeps decided
-> END

~ burn
Narrator: Brass curls and blackens in the iron stove, filling the room with a sharp metallic tang.
mori_shade [smile]: Let them come for their silver if they dare. My lungs feel clear for the first hour in a year.
set mori_outcome = "burn"
standing cult -2
quest what_mori_keeps decided
-> END

~ doris
Narrator: Constable Squire turns the paper in her gloved fingers, her face grey as slate.
doris_squire [neutral]: Keep your shop shuttered after the third bell, Mori. I will copy these into the ledger and walk the Round.
set mori_outcome = "doris"
standing old_ways -1
quest what_mori_keeps decided
-> END

~ silent
Narrator: The drawer slides shut with a soft wooden click, swallowing the faint gleam of brass.
mori_shade [weary]: Best let the village sleep easy. I will have the lamp trimmed before the next slip arrives.
set mori_outcome = "silent"
quest what_mori_keeps decided
-> END

~ later
Narrator: A newly struck brass plate rests on the workbench, metal filings still clinging to the letters.
mori_shade [afraid]: The monthly note came while you were at that dreadful house. They finally gave me a name for the blank plate.
set mori_later
quest what_mori_keeps done
-> END
